AiTask qa5_t09_country_revenue_diff {
  label: 'QA5 T09 Country Revenue Differences'
  description: 'Emails last full calendar month revenue by country, reporting only value and rank changes from the preceding completed run.'

  brief: @md
    Using @Dataset:ecommerce_official, run a fresh query in the workspace timezone. Calculate the dataset `revenue` metric for each country during the **most recently completed calendar month immediately before the task run date**. Group results by `countries.code` and `countries.name`; include every country with revenue in that reporting month. Exclude the current partial calendar month.

    Rank countries by unrounded revenue descending, breaking ties deterministically by `countries.code` ascending. Retain the precise, unrounded revenue for comparison and present revenue formatted as currency. Retrieve the full country-revenue table from the immediately preceding completed run of this same task, if one exists. The prior result must use this same reporting-month definition, revenue metric, grouping, ordering, and tie-breaker.

    If there is no preceding completed run, treat it as the first run: email the full current country table with country name, country code, rank, and revenue.

    If a preceding completed run exists, compare each current country to its preceding-run value and ordinal rank. Send an email that contains **only**: (1) countries whose precise revenue changed, showing prior revenue, current revenue, and the value difference; (2) countries whose ordinal rank changed, showing prior rank and current rank; and (3) countries newly present or no longer present, clearly labelled as added or removed. A country may appear once with all applicable changes. Do not include unchanged countries or the complete table in a non-first-run email.

    If no country revenue value, ordinal rank, or country membership changed, email a one-line message exactly stating that there was no change. On every run, use the available AI delivery capability to email **nhi.ty@holistics.io** exactly once. The email subject must begin exactly with **[QA5 T09]** and state the reporting month. Include the reporting month in the email body. Do not infer causes or make unsupported claims.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - A fresh query against @Dataset:ecommerce_official calculates the dataset `revenue` metric by `countries.code` and `countries.name` for the most recently completed calendar month immediately before the run date, in the workspace timezone; the current partial month is excluded.
    - Countries are ordered by unrounded revenue descending with `countries.code` ascending as the deterministic tie-breaker; each result preserves its precise revenue for comparisons and has an ordinal rank.
    - The current full country table is compared with the immediately preceding completed run of the same task using the identical metric, reporting-month definition, grouping, ordering, and tie-breaker.
    - On a definitively first run, exactly one email is delivered to nhi.ty@holistics.io with the full country table: country name, code, ordinal rank, and currency-formatted revenue.
    - On later runs with changes, exactly one email is delivered to nhi.ty@holistics.io containing only countries with a precise revenue change, ordinal-rank change, or added/removed membership. Revenue changes include prior value, current value, and difference; rank changes include prior and current rank; added and removed countries are labelled clearly. Unchanged countries are omitted.
    - If the two country tables are identical in membership, precise revenue values, and ordinal ranks, exactly one email is delivered containing a one-line no-change note.
    - Every email subject begins exactly with [QA5 T09] and identifies the reporting month; every body identifies the reporting month. All deliveries use the available AI delivery capability and contain no unsupported causal claims.
  ;;
}